v0.1.15 is now released.

This build ships 181 merged changes across the Stratos Crunch milestone. The =
headline work in this release is the backend expansion: batch-mode, bulk-llm-=
inference, caching-and-resume, local-offline-inference, multimodal-prompts, o=
nline-request-processing, and provider-integrations are all in flight and pro=
gressing well. The curator-viewer and progress-and-cli surface is also moving.

One thing worth flagging for anyone doing long runs: we found that appending =
to the input dataset between restarts is a trap. I added 200 rows to an 800-r=
ow set, restarted, and the resumed job came back with 800 results for 1000 re=
quests, then reassembly slotted them in by index. Half the rows ended up carr=
ying an answer to somebody else's question, and it looked completely fine on =
inspection. If you are resuming a job, do not change the input dataset betwee=
n runs.

Release notes from Emil are in progress. Shout if anything looks off.
